# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Payroll-tax API — environment
#
#   1. Copy this file:   cp .env.example .env
#   2. Paste your real values after each = below (no quotes, no spaces).
#   3. Run:              npm run api
#
# The server auto-loads .env on startup. .env is gitignored — your secrets
# never get committed. Leave a line blank to keep that feature off; with no
# Stripe keys the API runs in safe "ledger-only" mode (meters usage locally,
# charges nothing).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Stripe: the secret key (START IN TEST MODE) ──────────────────────────────
# Dashboard → Developers → API keys. Use the TEST key (sk_test_…) until you've
# charged a test card; a restricted key (rk_test_…) scoped to Customers,
# Checkout, PaymentIntents, Subscriptions and Billing Meters is even safer.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# ── Stripe: metered per-calculation billing ──────────────────────────────────
# Metering is ON only when a price id AND a meter event name are set (and
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY). With just a secret key, onboarding saves a card and
# nothing is metered. The rate is configured on the Stripe price. This app
# does not hardcode or display it.
# One-time setup in the Stripe Dashboard (test mode first):
#   Billing → Meters → create a meter; put its EVENT NAME below (it must match
#   exactly). STRIPE_METER_EVENT is still read if STRIPE_METER_EVENT_NAME is blank.
STRIPE_METER_EVENT_NAME=
STRIPE_METER_EVENT=
#   Then create a Product with a usage-based per-unit Price, monthly, tied to
#   that meter; paste its Price ID (price_…) below. Do not put the amount here.
STRIPE_PRICE_ID=
# Meter events that fail (Stripe down, network error) are queued in the store
# and retried every minute; nothing is dropped. See docs/GO-LIVE.md and
# `node scripts/meter-queue.ts` to inspect or flush the queue.

# ── Stripe: webhook signing secret (auto-suspend on failed payment) ──────────
# Dashboard → Developers → Webhooks → add endpoint. The SITE (npm run site) uses
# <PUBLIC_BASE_URL>/api/billing/webhook; the separate self-hosted API (npm run api) uses
# <PUBLIC_BASE_URL>/v1/billing/webhook. Full steps: docs/STRIPE-SETUP.md
# Endpoint URL: https://omniatax.io/api/billing/webhook
# Events: checkout.session.completed, customer.subscription.updated,
# customer.subscription.deleted, invoice.paid, invoice.payment_failed.
# Copy the "Signing secret" (whsec_…) it shows. Leave the value blank in git.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Live-mode Stripe secret keys (sk_live_ / rk_live_) are refused unless this is 1.
# Leave unset while using an sk_test_ key.
STRIPE_ALLOW_LIVE=

# ── Where this API is publicly reachable ─────────────────────────────────────
# Used to build the Stripe Checkout return links. REQUIRED in production. Left
# blank it falls back to http://localhost:<PORT> (never to the request's Host
# header, which a caller controls). An https value also marks the site's
# session cookie Secure.
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=

# Google Search Console HTML-tag verification. Paste only the token (the
# content value), not the whole meta tag. Leave this unset until Search
# Console issues one: the site then omits the tag. A token must match
# [A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,128} or it is ignored.
GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Port the API listens on (default 4380).
PORT=4380
# Where the key + usage store is written (default api/.data).
# API_DB_DIR=/var/lib/payroll-api
# Keys are minted as sk_test_ unless you pass --live or set this to 1.
# API_ISSUE_LIVE_KEYS=1

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Omnia site server (npm run site — the landing page, console, and public API)
#
# The same .env is loaded by the site server. These configure it; all are
# optional and have safe defaults, so `npm run site` works with none of them.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the site's account/key/usage store is written. Point this at a durable,
# backed-up volume in production; default is site/.data (gitignored, ephemeral).
# SITE_DB_DIR=/var/lib/omnia

# Per-key rate limit for POST /api/paycheck, requests per minute (default 120).
# RATE_LIMIT_PER_MIN=120

# Cap on retained usage-log events before the oldest are trimmed (default 50000).
# Per-key lifetime totals are tracked separately and are never lost to trimming.
# MAX_USAGE_EVENTS=50000

# Set to 1 to mint production keys with an sk_live_ prefix instead of sk_test_.
# Leave unset during evaluation.
# OMNIA_ISSUE_LIVE_KEYS=1

# Signup and sign-in code requests allowed per client address per hour
# (default 10 each). Stored in the site store, so they survive restarts and
# are shared by instances on the same volume. Set TRUST_PROXY=1 behind a
# reverse proxy so the client address comes from X-Forwarded-For.
# Checkout uses the dynamic payment methods enabled in the Stripe Dashboard.
# Do not send payment_method_types; Stripe API 2026-09-30.endive rejects it.

# SIGNUP_PER_HOUR=10
# SIGNIN_PER_HOUR=10
# TRUST_PROXY=1
# On Render, the platform sets RENDER. That is treated as TRUST_PROXY for
# the client address (rate limits) and as a reason to mark the session
# cookie Secure. Set TRUST_PROXY=0 to refuse X-Forwarded-For anyway.

# Metered billing for the site (uses the same STRIPE_* values above):
#   - STRIPE_PRICE_ID must be a usage-metered price. The rate is set in Stripe.
#     With it set, onboarding creates a subscription (with the free trial) and
#     every successful live paycheck calculation reports one meter event.
#   - STRIPE_METER_EVENT_NAME is the billing-meter event name. REQUIRED for
#     metering — there is no default, because events under a name no meter
#     listens for bill nothing.
#   - STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET verifies POST https://omniatax.io/api/billing/webhook
#     over the raw body. A failed invoice suspends a key; a paid invoice
#     reactivates it. Deliveries are idempotent on the Stripe event id.
#   - Sandbox keys (sk_test_) are not metered. A live Stripe secret
#     (sk_live_) is refused unless STRIPE_ALLOW_LIVE=1.

# Public https URL of the site, for Stripe Checkout return links
# (falls back to http://localhost:PORT). PUBLIC_BASE_URL above is shared.

# Transactional email for the 6-digit signup verification code (Resend). With no
# key set (local development only), the code is printed to the server console
# instead of emailed. With a key set, codes are never written to logs.
# RESEND_API_KEY=

# The site server listens on PORT too (its own default is 4323 when PORT unset).

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Python email verifier (npm run verifier). Optional: when VERIFIER_URL and
# VERIFIER_SECRET are set on the site, the verifier mints, mails and checks the
# 6-digit codes, stores only HMAC hashes of them, and the site's own store never
# holds a code. Leave them unset to use the site's built-in verification.
#
# Generate both secrets with:  python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared by the site and the verifier (>= 32 chars). Sent as a Bearer token.
# VERIFIER_SECRET=
# Verifier only (>= 32 chars). Keys the stored code hashes.
# VERIFIER_PEPPER=
# Site only: where the verifier listens.
# VERIFIER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4390
# Verifier only: VERIFIER_PORT=4390  VERIFIER_DB=/var/lib/omnia/verifier.sqlite3
# Mail transport (first one set wins): RESEND_API_KEY above, or
# SMTP_HOST= SMTP_PORT=587 SMTP_USER= SMTP_PASS= SMTP_FROM=
# Local development only, with no mail transport: VERIFIER_DEV=1 prints codes to stderr.
# The signup page mentions the server log only when NODE_ENV is not production,
# or when OMNIA_DEV_CODE_HINT=1 (or VERIFIER_DEV=1) is set on the site process.
# Leave both unset in production.
# OMNIA_DEV_CODE_HINT=

# Large local address index (keyed-API geocoding only; the public website lookup never reads it).
# ADDRESS_INDEX_PATH is where it lives; deploy/start.sh fetches or builds it in the background.
# ADDRESS_INDEX_PATH=/var/data/address-index/address-points.db
# A prebuilt index to download (address-points.db or .db.gz) and its sha256:
# ADDRESS_INDEX_URL=
# ADDRESS_INDEX_SHA256=
# Or build it on the server from OpenAddresses (hours on a small instance, ~20 GB free disk needed):
# ADDRESS_INDEX_AUTOBUILD=1

# ── Contact form ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where messages from /contact are emailed (through the same Resend account as
# verification codes, so RESEND_API_KEY must be set). Defaults to the address
# printed on the contact page. Without RESEND_API_KEY the form falls back to
# opening the visitor's own mail app.
# CONTACT_TO=you@yourdomain.com

# Account backup in Stripe (used when the site's disk is temporary and STRIPE_SECRET_KEY is set).
# Pin the encryption key so rotating the Stripe key never strands the backups. STORE_MIRROR=0 turns it off.
# STORE_MIRROR_SECRET=
